{"step_index":1211,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-05T06:32:53Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-05T00:32:53-06:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-05T00:32:56-06:00\nCommand exited with code 0.\n\nCommand output:\nC:\\Users\\andre\\OneDrive\\Desktop\\xview\\experimento\\08_device_trees_uboot_y_configs_firmware\\aml_upgrade_package.conf\nC:\\Users\\andre\\OneDrive\\Desktop\\xview\\experimento\\08_device_trees_uboot_y_configs_firmware\\meson-g12-common.dtsi\nC:\\Users\\andre\\OneDrive\\Desktop\\xview\\experimento\\08_device_trees_uboot_y_configs_firmware\\meson-g12a-u200.dts\nC:\\Users\\andre\\OneDrive\\Desktop\\xview\\experimento\\08_device_trees_uboot_y_configs_firmware\\meson-g12a-x96-max.dts\nC:\\Users\\andre\\OneDrive\\Desktop\\xview\\experimento\\08_device_trees_uboot_y_configs_firmware\\meson-g12a.dtsi\nC:\\Users\\andre\\OneDrive\\Desktop\\xview\\experimento\\08_device_trees_uboot_y_configs_firmware\\meson-s4.dtsi\nC:\\Users\\andre\\OneDrive\\Desktop\\xview\\experimento\\08_device_trees_uboot_y_configs_firmware\\optimizar_imagen_y_hdmi_xview.bat\nC:\\Users\\andre\\OneDrive\\Desktop\\xview\\experimento\\08_device_trees_uboot_y_configs_firmware\\uboot_env_franklin_b866v2.cfg\n# ==============================================================================\r\n# CONFIGURACIÃ“N DE ENTORNO U-BOOT (env) â€” ZTE ZXV10 B866V2 (Placa: franklin / g12a)\r\n# Procesador: Amlogic S905X2 | Memoria: 2GB DDR4 + 8GB eMMC | Wi-Fi: MT7661LSN\r\n# ==============================================================================\r\n\r\nbaudrate=115200\r\nboard=franklin\r\nsoc=g12a\r\narch=arm\r\ncpu=armv8\r\n\r\n# ParÃ¡metros de salida de video HDMI y espacio de color (Amlogic VOUT / HDMITX)\r\nhdmimode=1080p60hz\r\noutputmode=1080p60hz\r\ncolorattribute=444,8bit\r\ndolby_status=0\r\nhdr_policy=1\r\nfrac_rate_policy=1\r\n\r\n# ResoluciÃ³n del Framebuffer de interfaz (OSD)\r\nfb_width=1920\r\nfb_height=1080\r\ndisplay_bpp=32\r\ndisplay_color_index=32\r\ndisplay_layer=osd0\r\n\r\n# Argumentos pasados al Kernel Linux (cmdline)\r\ninitargs=rootfstype=ramfs init=/init console=ttyS0,115200 no_console_suspend earlycon=aml-uart,0xff803000 ramoops.pstore_en=1 ramoops.record_size=0x8000 ramoops.console_size=0x4000\r\n\r\n# Comandos de arranque estÃ¡ndar (Android 12 en eMMC)\r\nstoreboot=imgread kernel boot ${loadaddr}; bootm ${loadaddr};\r\n\r\n# ConfiguraciÃ³n de Multiboot por USB / SD (Armbian / Debian / CoreELEC / EmuELEC)\r\n# Basado en mirko-geno/b866v2-debian y ophub/amlogic-s9xxx-armbian\r\nstart_autoscript=if usb start; then run start_usb_autoscript; fi; if mmcinfo; then run start_mmc_autoscript; fi;\r\nstart_usb_autoscript=if fatload usb 0 1020000 s905_autoscript; then autoscr 1020000; fi; if fatload usb 1 1020000 s905_autoscript; then autoscr 1020000; fi;\r\nstart_mmc_autoscript=if fatload mmc 0 1020000 s905_autoscript; then autoscr 1020000; fi;\r\n"}
{"step_index":1212,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-05T06:32:56Z","input_tokens":3395,"cache_read_tokens":246376,"output_tokens":1472,"thinking":"The failure of both units after the same command suggests a shared cause. The `fastboot flash` command, specifically targeting the `env` partition, is the likely culprit. This implicates the environment variables, which control device behavior during boot. Investigating the impact of this particular `env` image is critical.\n\n\nThe absence of `init_display` in the modified `env` image prevents HDMI initialization, explaining the \"no signal\" error. Furthermore, the missing `storeargs` command results in an empty `bootargs` variable passed to the kernel, affecting boot parameters. This likely causes the device to fail to boot properly, explaining why it cannot fully initialize.\n\n\nThe missing `init_display`, `storeargs`, and other environment variables prevent proper HDMI initialization and boot parameter setup. The environment variables are crucial for the boot process. Investigating what happens in the absence of a valid environment partition may reveal how to restore the boot process. If `/dev/block/env` is erased or corrupted, the system falls back to a default environment embedded in `bootloader.img`. This embedded environment contains the missing variables.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"$blFile = \\\"c:\\\\Users\\\\andre\\\\OneDrive\\\\Desktop\\\\xview\\\\normal\\\\B866V2\\\\bootloader.img\\\"\\n$bytes = [System.IO.File]::ReadAllBytes($blFile)\\nWrite-Host \\\"bootloader.img size: $($bytes.Length)\\\"\\nfor ($i = 0; $i -lt $bytes.Length - 4; $i++) {\\n    # GZIP magic: 1F 8B 08\\n    if ($bytes[$i] -eq 0x1F -and $bytes[$i+1] -eq 0x8B -and $bytes[$i+2] -eq 0x08) {\\n        Write-Host \\\"GZIP header @ 0x$($i.ToString('X'))\\\"\\n    }\\n    # LZ4 frame magic: 04 22 4D 18\\n    if ($bytes[$i] -eq 0x04 -and $bytes[$i+1] -eq 0x22 -and $bytes[$i+2] -eq 0x4D -and $bytes[$i+3] -eq 0x18) {\\n        Write-Host \\\"LZ4 header @ 0x$($i.ToString('X'))\\\"\\n    }\\n    # AML FIP / TOC / LZO / XZ\\n    if ($bytes[$i] -eq 0xFD -and $bytes[$i+1] -eq 0x37 -and $bytes[$i+2] -eq 0x7A -and $bytes[$i+3] -eq 0x58) {\\n        Write-Host \\\"XZ header @ 0x$($i.ToString('X'))\\\"\\n    }\\n}\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolSummary":"\"Find compressed BL33 payload offset inside bootloader.img\""}}]}
